{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>For you did YHWH your Elohim choose to be His treasured people</b> — there is no officer, magistrate, or ruler over all the supernal angels, but you are the סגולה (treasured possession) of YHWH directly under His hand. Therefore you will not go astray to worship idolatry from the elohim of the peoples, and I have already mentioned this many times. And this is the reason for \"not because you are more numerous than all the peoples\" — for it would have been fitting that the many belong to the King, as it is written (Proverbs 14:28), \"In the multitude of people is the glory of a king,\" and that He appoint commanders of hosts at the head of those who remain, while you are the few — yet even so He desired you and chose you."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:46:30.668209394Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}